  "worked_solution": "First, we add and subtract $4$ in the numerator. This reveals a copy of the denominator without changing the value of the expression.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8{x}^{5}-9}{8{x}^{5}+4}\\,=\\,\\frac{8{x}^{5}+4-4-9}{8{x}^{5}+4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we split the fraction into two, and then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8{x}^{5}+4-4-9}{8{x}^{5}+4} & =\\frac{8{x}^{5}+4}{8{x}^{5}+4}+\\frac{-4-9}{8{x}^{5}+4} \\\\  & =1+\\frac{-13}{8{x}^{5}+4}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
